RULES = [
 ('R01','F01','Extra Help application route',
  'Medicare Part A or Part B or both, residence, income and resources, application and actual Part D/MA-PD enrollment conditions remain attached. A determination can occur before drug-plan enrollment; receiving the subsidy requires that enrollment. This is not a Medicaid determination.',
  ['ssa-0603001020:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3101','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3110']),
 ('R02','F07','Deemed Extra Help is a separate route',
  'Medicare drug-eligible beneficiaries receiving full-benefit Medicaid, SSI, QMB, SLMB or QI can be deemed without a separate Extra Help application. Require actual qualifying status, not an application or a user guess. QDWI alone is excluded. Part B-ID alone does not establish Part D eligibility.',
  ['ssa-0603010005:ALL','ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.773','cms-buyin:PAGE:12']),
 ('R03','F07','Deemed period and reapplication',
  'Deemed between January 1 and June 30: at least the remainder of the year. Deemed between July 1 and December 31: remainder of that year and the following year. Notices and changes are handled by CMS/SSA; loss of deemed status is not a blanket lifetime loss of assistance.',
  ['ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.773','ssa-0603010005:ALL']),
 ('R04','F03','Extra Help family size and whose money counts',
  'Applicant, living-with spouse and co-resident relatives supported at least one-half define the Extra Help family size. A supported relative can increase the FPL household size without adding that relative income/resources. Married living-together spouse income/resources count even if only one applies; separations and temporary absences have specific rules. Do not substitute tax household size.',
  ['ssa-0603020055:ALL','ssa-0603020010:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3310']),
 ('R05','F03','Annual versus monthly income and gross amounts',
  'Extra Help uses countable income with the applicable annual/partial-year projection rules. Florida MSSI uses monthly prospective budgeting. Social Security before the Part B withholding and other gross receipts are not the same as bank deposits or final countable income. No annual personal total is inferred from a single quoted threshold.',
  ['ssa-0603020015:ALL','ssa-0603020055:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3320','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0201']),
 ('R06','F05','Florida standard and earned income disregards',
  'The applicable MSSI standard disregard is $20 per month, not doubled for a couple; apply first to unearned income, then any unused amount to earned income. The separate earned-income disregard is $65 plus one-half of remaining earned income. Need-based income and other exceptions remain in the complete passages. These amounts do not make all gross income countable.',
  ['dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0321','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0322','fac-chapter:RULE:65A-1.713']),
 ('R07','F05','Extra Help income exclusions',
  'Retain the complete SSA earned/unearned exclusion lists and their exceptions, including general income exclusion, earned-income treatment, interest/dividends and in-kind support/maintenance. PASS is not newly approved merely to qualify for Extra Help. SSI similarities do not make every SSI or Florida rule interchangeable.',
  ['ssa-0603020030:ALL','ssa-0603020050:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3350']),
 ('R08','F06','Extra Help resources and timing',
  'Count applicant/living-with spouse resources under the Extra Help definitions and applicable timing, including liquid resources, non-home real-property equity and specified trust rules. Retain exclusions for the principal home, vehicles/household items where applicable, life-insurance cash surrender value and non-liquid resources. Do not use total net worth or import Medicaid transfer penalties into Extra Help.',
  ['ssa-0603030001:ALL','ssa-0603030020:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3405']),
 ('R09','F06','Base and burial-adjusted LIS resource displays',
  'The 2026 base limits are $16,590/$33,100; $18,090/$36,100 include the $1,500-per-person burial exclusion when applicable. They express different bases, not a source conflict. Preserve whether none/one/both spouses expect burial use. Do not deduct the exclusion and also compare against an already adjusted display.',
  ['cms-lis-2026:PAGE:1','cms-lis-2026:PAGE:3','ssa-0603030020:ALL','ssa-0603030025:ALL']),
 ('R10','F11','LIS strict income and non-strict resource endpoints',
  'The operative federal law, 42 CFR 423.773 and SSA resource tables require income below 150% FPL for the application route and resources at or below the applicable standard. CMS table shorthand using less-than-or-equal income does not override operative below wording. Exact equality is retained as a source comparison, not a personal denial.',
  ['usc-lis:ALL','ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.773','ssa-0603030025:ALL','cms-lis-2026:PAGE:4']),
 ('R11','F11','SSA income note does not waive the resource requirement',
  'One HI 03020.055 note says full subsidy regardless of whether resources are under the limit. Its surrounding policy, HI 03001.020, HI 03030.025, statute and regulations require both for applicants unless separately deemed. Preserve the contradictory note and do not implement it as a new resource-free route.',
  ['ssa-0603020055:ALL','ssa-0603001020:ALL','ssa-0603030025:ALL','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3101','ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.773']),
 ('R12','F08','Full subsidy and premium ceiling',
  'Current Extra Help provides full subsidy under the applicable post-2023 rules. Full subsidy covers the defined basic premium subsidy amount, subject to the benchmark/lowest-basic-premium rule and applicable de minimis waiver; it does not guarantee every selected plan premium or enhanced benefit premium is zero. Plan-specific net premiums remain L04/L06 evidence, not invented here.',
  ['ssa-0603001020:ALL','ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.780']),
 ('R13','F08','2026 maximum covered-drug cost sharing',
  'CMS 2026 category-specific maxima are retained: institutional/qualifying HCBS full-benefit duals $0; other full-benefit duals at or below 100% FPL $1.60 generic/$4.90 brand; remaining listed full-subsidy categories $5.10/$12.65, with $0 deductible. Covered Part D cost sharing above the $2,100 out-of-pocket threshold is zero. These are maxima with exact category/covered-drug conditions, not pharmacy prices or prices for noncovered drugs.',
  ['cms-lis-2026:PAGE:4']),
 ('R14','F08','No current partial-subsidy schedule or penalty',
  'The old partial subsidy bands apply to pre-2024 effective awards, not a new 2026 sliding benefit. Retain historical source tables as context. Eligible Extra Help beneficiaries have the applicable Part D late-penalty waiver. Wider enrollment timing remains L13; stale POMS rolling MA-PD wording is not adopted as a current unlimited MA switching rule.',
  ['ssa-0603001005:ALL','ssa-0603001010:ALL','ecfr-lis-cms-1027:CFR:423.780']),
 ('R15','F01','QMB benefits and actual Medicare status',
  'QMB assists with applicable Part A/Part B premiums and Medicare cost sharing. Retain Part A/conditional enrollment and technical requirements, plus the distinct Part B-ID variant. QMB-only is limited Medicaid; QMB-plus separately qualifies for full Medicaid. No patient is made full-benefit dual from a QMB-only label.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0817','dcf-1430:SECTION:1440.1504','cms-buyin:PAGE:32','cms-buyin:PAGE:33']),
 ('R16','F01','SLMB and QI benefits and limits',
  'SLMB and QI pay the relevant Part B premium; they do not by themselves cover all A/B deductibles and coinsurance. SLMB-plus requires separate full Medicaid eligibility. QI has finite federal funding, annual selection/prior-recipient rules and no QI-plus category. Florida wording retains its Medically Needy exception; do not collapse it into unconditional simultaneous full Medicaid.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0818','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0819','cms-buyin:PAGE:35','cms-buyin:PAGE:36','cms-buyin:PAGE:37']),
 ('R17','F02','Florida published MSP countable standards',
  'Retain all family-size, blank-resource and additional-person cells in both the April and interim January 2026 A-9.1 tables. Use the April table as the retained current standard at the October reference date. DCF transmittal I-25-12-0013 explicitly explains the interim 2.8% increase; its attached January table matches all 48 printed numeric cells. Staff were instructed not to close Medicaid cases using interim FPL figures before the spring standards. Retain published amounts; do not replace them with a speculative rounding formula.',
  ['dcf-a91-reused:PAGE:1','dcf-cola-2026-archive:PAGE:2','dcf-cola-2026-archive:PAGE:4','dcf-cola-2026-archive:PAGE:12','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0112','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0114','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0115']),
 ('R18','F11','Federal gross summaries versus state countable standards',
  'SSA national QMB/SLMB/QI summaries include the $20 general disregard; Florida A-9.1 reports the lower countable standards. The six individual/couple comparisons reconcile exactly after adding $20. Earned-income cases can differ further. QDWI gross summaries also incorporate earned-income exclusions and are not directly comparable to the Florida 200% countable standard.',
  ['ssa-0600815023:ALL','dcf-a91-reused:PAGE:1','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0321','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0322']),
 ('R19','F04','Florida filing unit and deemed family money',
  'Retain MSSI individual/eligible-couple, living-with spouse, parent/child deeming and institutional spousal exceptions. An assistance-group member differs from a standard-filing-unit member. Do not use Extra Help supported-relative family size as a Florida Medicaid household test or assume every co-resident income counts.',
  ['dcf-2200:SECTION:2240.0200','dcf-2200:SECTION:2240.0600','dcf-2200:SECTION:2240.0604.03','dcf-2200:SECTION:2240.0604.04','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0212','dcf-2600:ALL']),
 ('R20','F06','Florida MSSI resource exclusions are program-specific',
  'Adopted .712 and the asset chapter retain ownership/availability, a home exclusion and its institutional qualifications, a vehicle, life-insurance face-value/CSV conditions, designated burial funds and other exclusions. Florida burial designation up to $2,500 each is not the Extra Help $1,500 rule. Trust/annuity/transfer and spousal allocation require exact program evidence and agency/specialist application.',
  ['fac-chapter:RULE:65A-1.712','dcf-1630:SECTION:1640.0205','dcf-1630:ALL']),
 ('R21','F01','Working-disabled Medicare Part A premium route',
  'Florida Working Disabled corresponds to the qualified working-disabled Part A premium route: under 65, medically disabled/working, lost premium-free entitlement and special extended Part A enrollment confirmed by SSA, plus income/resource/technical conditions. It is not the HCBS Working People with Disabilities program and does not itself deem Extra Help.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0816','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0113','ssa-0603010005:ALL','cms-buyin:PAGE:56']),
 ('R22','F11','Florida working-disabled resource discrepancy',
  'Coverage passage 2040.0816 says $4,000/$6,000. The adopted .712(1)(c) uses the Medically Needy resource limit, .716(3) states $5,000/$6,000, and current asset passage 1640.0205 and A-9 agree. Retain $5,000/$6,000 as the Florida published reference with all contrary observations visible; the federal national floor remains $4,000/$6,000. Qualified review must confirm consequential state/federal application before any personal decision.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0816','dcf-1630:SECTION:1640.0205','fac-chapter:RULE:65A-1.712','fac-chapter:RULE:65A-1.716','dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1','ssa-0600815023:ALL']),
 ('R23','F09','SSI and protected Medicaid pathways',
  'Retain SSI-linked coverage, COLA/Pickle protection and disabled-adult-child protection with exact conditions. SSDI is not SSI. Historical widow/child groups and groups that end at Medicare Part A remain visible with limitations. No generic rule that every low-income Medicare beneficiary qualifies for full Medicaid.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0801.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0802.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0804.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0806.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0807.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0808','dcf-2400:SECTION:2440.0105']),
 ('R24','F09','MEDS-AD Medicare restriction',
  'The 88%-FPL MEDS-AD financial row alone is not an ordinary full-Medicaid path for every Medicare beneficiary. The coverage passage requires no Medicare, or, for a Medicare recipient, receiving qualifying institutional, hospice or HCBS services, with the stated assessment/enrollment conditions. Preserve these limits next to the amount.',
  ['dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0813.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0813.02','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0813.03','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0813.04','dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1']),
 ('R25','F09','Medically Needy share-of-cost reference',
  'The $180/$241 values are monthly Medically Needy income levels used in share-of-cost budgeting, not gross-income eligibility caps. There is no stated gross-income cap in the A-9 row. Actual eligibility depends on countable income, allowed expenses, resource/technical conditions and meeting the share of cost; HCBS does not use the Medically Needy route. Do not promise full Medicaid/LIS from unmet spend-down status.',
  ['dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1','fac-chapter:RULE:65A-1.713','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0815.01','dcf-2600:ALL']),
 ('R26','F09','Institutional/HCBS/hospice financial and assessment boundaries',
  'Retain ICP/HCBS/hospice/PACE standards and alternatives at the applicable periods, but separate individual/couple, MEDS-AD asset alternatives, assessments, level of care, available waiver services, trusts/transfers and spousal impoverishment. A published amount does not establish admission, a waiver slot or eligibility. Clinical/service-path details remain L08/L14/agency evidence.',
  ['dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0801.05','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0814.01','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0814.02','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0815.01','dcf-1630:SECTION:1640.0205']),
 ('R27','F11','May 2026 Working People with Disabilities law',
  'The WPwD program predates 2026; DCF says it began January 1, 2020. Chapter 2026-88 took effect May 21, 2026 and contains specific developmental-disability, current HCBS-waiver, age-18+, employment/earned-income conditions for automatic enrollment and optional participation. DCF current operational guidance describes a broader disability/HCBS-waiver route. Preserve both scopes without denying existing non-developmental-disability routes. The January attachment already prints the $13,000/$24,000 asset disregard, so May 21 is not an inferred introduction date for those financial amounts. Retain 550% SSI FBR, the law retirement-account exclusion and old manual limit wording; do not substitute an asset ceiling for a disregard. Exact broader automatic-enrollment application remains qualified review.',
  ['law-2026-88:PAGE:1','law-2026-88:PAGE:2','dcf-medicaid-landing:ALL','dcf-cola-2026-archive:PAGE:11','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0815.01','dcf-1630:SECTION:1640.0205','dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1']),
 ('R28','F02','January/April/July standards are distinct',
  'The A-9 footnotes identify January annual, April FPL-based and July spousal-maintenance updates. Both the current July table and dated January attachment are retained with per-row units/bases, including the dated 2025 transfer divisor. The January attachment has student exclusion figures $2,416/$9,460, conflicting with SSA and the current DCF $2,410 monthly/$9,730 annual. Use the latter as the 2026 reference and preserve the incorrect earlier observation. Do not substitute current FPL/spousal amounts for earlier dates; the exact DCF correction/change instruction remains unlocated for retrospective agency reproduction.',
  ['dcf-a9-current:PAGE:1','dcf-cola-2026-archive:PAGE:11','ssa-0500820510:ALL','dcf-31191:PAGE:1','dcf-31196:PAGE:1']),
 ('R29','F10','Agency applications and cross-referral',
  'SSA or state Medicaid application routes and official notices determine assistance. The Extra Help application can initiate the MSP process unless the person opts out, but it is not an approval for MSP/full Medicaid. Confirmed/deemed status and actual Part D enrollment remain distinct from filing. Daylight files no application and collects no personal financial information in this reference.',
  ['ssa-0603010010:ALL','ssa-0603010005:ALL','ssa-0603010020:ALL','dcf-600:ALL','dcf-help-landing:ALL']),
 ('R30','F10','Coverage start, buy-in and retroactivity',
  'QMB has a distinct effective-date rule with CMS-described state flexibility in the determination month; the precise Florida election is not verified here. SLMB may have up to three months retroactivity; QI may have up to three but not into a previous calendar year, under the stated conditions. Buy-in transmission/refund timing differs from eligibility start. Florida adult Medicaid retroactivity restrictions are not silently overridden by older generic three-month manual wording.',
  ['cms-buyin:PAGE:33','cms-buyin:PAGE:36','cms-buyin:PAGE:37','ssa-0600815018:ALL','dcf-600:SECTION:0640.0509','dcf-2000:SECTION:2040.0812.02']),
 ('R31','F01','QMB billing protection',
  'Medicare providers and suppliers must not bill QMB beneficiaries for covered Part A/B cost sharing, including in MA; protection does not depend on provider Medicaid enrollment or state payment. Retain covered-service, verification, permitted Medicaid-copay and noncovered-service distinctions. This is not a promise of all care free.',
  ['cms-qmb-billing:PAGE:2','cms-qmb-billing:PAGE:3','cms-dual-guide-current:PAGE:7']),
 ('R32','F10','Collier and statewide counseling route',
  'Retain official SHINE statewide telephone/TTY and the current Collier directory route with appointment/member limitations preserved in source text. These are referral routes, not a booked appointment, service availability guarantee or permission to contact anyone.',
  ['shine-contact:ALL','shine-collier:ALL']),
 ('R33','F12','Unknowns and independent review',
  'No unknown input becomes a denial or poor fit. Source-native conflicts, historical gaps and program variants remain visible. Financial standards and synthetic checks are not an agency eligibility determination, an independently accepted exhaustive rule engine, qualified R17 review or exact owner acceptance. No consumer release or recommendation gate is changed.',
  ['ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3110','dcf-help-landing:ALL']),
 ('R34','F01','Part B-ID assistance variants',
  'QMB, SLMB and QI have limited Part B-ID assistance variants under the stated qualifying conditions. QMB Part B-ID helps the limited premium/cost-sharing; SLMB/QI Part B-ID help that premium only. This immunosuppressive-drug-only benefit is not full Medicare Part B and does not by itself establish Part D/Extra Help eligibility or a general plan enrollment right.',
  ['cms-buyin:PAGE:12','cms-buyin:PAGE:32','cms-buyin:PAGE:33','cms-buyin:PAGE:35','cms-buyin:PAGE:36','ecfr-lis-ssa-1027:CFR:418.3101']),
]

